## Context and authority

Child of1572, finding4. The author’s interface session /root relayed approval
of this proposed choice rule: use the central claim from the original abstract
and introduction, then its supporting table/figure, before package inspection
or execution; for equally ranked central results, the driver prospectively
records a motivated choice under a consistent cohort rule.

Actual author reply as relayed:

> D’accord. Ne pas hésiter à utiliser le advisor model, c’est une étape clé. Elsevier demande des key findings aux articles récents, penser à regarder en ligne si ils y sont.

## Scope

Implement original-paper-led main-result choice with proportionate route-advisor
support for pivotal judgment. Actually consult a distinct advisor when designing
this guidance; do not self-certify that requirement. At skill application, inspect
article-specific Highlights/Key findings on the official original-article page
when present, crosschecking abstract/introduction and main supporting evidence.
Do not assert that every recent Elsevier article has these. In blind mode use
only the supplied original-paper route and preserve existing answer exclusions;
missing/inaccessible highlights are reported, not permission for discovery.
Package availability never chooses the main result. Driver/cohort selection
policy is prospective and motivated, without hard-coded project names. No new
pipeline, scientific execution, automatic legacy selection/rescore, or changed
comparison/scoring categories are authorized by this documentation child.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Main-result choice follows original central claim and supporting evidence before package inspection/execution, with prospective motivated tie choice and cohort consistency.
- [ ] Proportionate advisor use is specified for pivotal judgment, and a real distinct advisor report informs this guidance design.
- [ ] Optional official article Highlights/Key findings are crosschecked without universal publisher claims or new blind discovery authority; inaccessible evidence stays explicit.
- [ ] Parallel guidance preserves canonical/selected scope, comparison rules, and prior case records without automatic legacy reselection/rescore or a package-led choice.

## Plan and first verification

Documentation contract. Read current assess/main-result/selected-target units
and the recorded ruling, consult the route advisor, then write a source/scenario
audit: central result visible but package incomplete (positive control against
package-led selection), equally central results, optional highlights agreeing or
conflicting with article text, absent/inaccessible original page, and a blind
supplied route that must not open replication answers. No wording-pin tests or
scientific estimates. Required adherence, distinct semantic review, gaze, gate,
pinned merge, and roar follow the live skills.

## Feasibility

PASS: local documentation surfaces exist; guidance design needs no article
crawl or paid API. Advisor must use an authorized subscription/private route.
Actual article-page lookup belongs to later paper selection. Sequential after
1584 because shared SKILL/reference contracts. No implementation has begun.
